+# Correcting a Booked Visit Is In Scope; Cancelling Stays Out
+
+**Status:** Accepted. Narrows NG-5 as recorded in [Deleting Records and Amending Booked Visits Are Deliberately Out of Scope](2026-08-08-non-goal-deletion-and-visit-amendment.md).
+
+## Context
+
+NG-5 read "Changing or cancelling a visit once booked". The 2026-08-08 ADR confirmed it deliberate, alongside NG-4. That ADR set two conditions on the row. A request touching it proceeds only on an explicit owner decision recorded at intake, and narrowing it later takes its own non-goal ADR.
+
+The owner has now decided (2026-08-11). Correcting a booked visit's date and description is in scope; cancelling one is not.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Leave NG-5 whole.** Rejected: the owner has decided, and the 2026-08-08 ADR names this decision as the way the row moves.
+2. **Retire NG-5 entirely.** Open both correction and cancellation. Rejected: the owner scoped only correction. Cancellation carries the cascading-removal questions NG-4 keeps out, and it would add the lifecycle state the original rationale declined.
+3. **Narrow NG-5 to cancellation alone** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+A booked visit's date and description can be corrected, recorded as [REQ-VIS-003](../prd.md#req-vis-003). A correction replaces the existing visit rather than recording a second one, and is held to the same rules as booking.
+
+Cancelling a booked visit stays out of scope. NG-5 now reads "Cancelling a visit once booked". The NG-4 half of the 2026-08-08 ADR is untouched and stands.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The sample demonstrates forward correction on the visit record, as it already does for owner and pet details.
+- Cancellation and deletion remain out. A reader who wants to undo a visit still cannot.
+- A visit whose date has passed cannot be corrected while keeping that date, because the booking date rule applies unchanged.
+- The correction form is reachable by its address alone. The owner's record gains no visible way to reach it in this slice, which is a deliberate boundary and an open question.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-5
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row.
+- [REQ-VIS-003](../prd.md#req-vis-003) — the capability the narrowing admits.
+
+## References
+
+- [Deleting Records and Amending Booked Visits Are Deliberately Out of Scope](2026-08-08-non-goal-deletion-and-visit-amendment.md) — the decision this narrows.
